const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"把错误放在所有发现中衡量",en:"Measure errors among the discoveries"},body:{zh:"Benjamini与Hochberg将错误拒绝的数量除以全部拒绝的数量，并对这个随机比例取期望。如果没有任何拒绝，比例定义为零。分母不是全部检验数，因此FDR与每个检验的错误率是不同指标，不能仅因都写成百分比就混用。",en:"The authors take the expected proportion of false rejections among all rejections, defining the proportion as zero when none are rejected. The denominator is not the number of tests. FDR and per-test error rates remain different quantities even when both are percentages."},reference:{url:"https://www.dcscience.net/Benjamini-Hochberg-1995-FDR.pdf",label:{zh:"1995年期刊版 · §2.1",en:"1995 journal article · §2.1"}}},{title:{zh:"与至少错一次的概率不同",en:"It differs from the probability of any error"},body:{zh:"家族错误率关注是否至少出现一次错误拒绝，FDR则关注错误在发现中所占的比例。全部原假设都为真时，两者一致；存在真实效应时，FDR通常允许更宽松的筛选。是否接受这种取舍，应由研究的决策后果决定。",en:"Familywise error concerns whether any false rejection occurs; FDR concerns the proportion among discoveries. They coincide when every null is true. When real effects exist, FDR can support less stringent screening, but the consequences of errors determine whether that tradeoff is suitable."},reference:{url:"https://www.dcscience.net/Benjamini-Hochberg-1995-FDR.pdf",label:{zh:"1995年期刊版 · §2.1",en:"1995 journal article · §2.1"}}},{title:{zh:"期望比例不是每批结果的保证",en:"An expected proportion is not a guarantee for each batch"},body:{zh:"论文明确区分随机比例、比例的期望以及两个期望之比。FDR控制并不意味着某一次筛选中错误发现必然少于指定百分比，也不为每个入选结论分配一个可信概率。解读结果时，应保留这种重复实验层面的含义。",en:"The paper separates the random proportion, its expectation and ratios of expectations. FDR control does not guarantee that every realized batch stays below the target proportion, nor assign a credibility probability to each selected result. Its meaning is across repeated experiments."},reference:{url:"https://www.dcscience.net/Benjamini-Hochberg-1995-FDR.pdf",label:{zh:"1995年期刊版 · §2.3",en:"1995 journal article · §2.3"}}},{title:{zh:"排序后寻找最后一个满足条件的位置",en:"Find the last qualifying ordered p-value"},body:{zh:"程序把m个p值从小到大排列，找到满足p值不超过i乘目标水平再除以m的最大位置k，并拒绝排序前k个假设。如果没有位置满足条件，就不拒绝任何假设。这里是逐步向上的整体规则，不是每个p值都与同一门槛比较。",en:"Order m p-values and find the largest rank k whose p-value is at most k times the target level divided by m; reject through that rank. If none qualifies, reject none. This step-up rule differs from applying one identical threshold to every test."},reference:{url:"https://www.dcscience.net/Benjamini-Hochberg-1995-FDR.pdf",label:{zh:"1995年期刊版 · §3.1 · procedure (1)",en:"1995 journal article · §3.1 · procedure (1)"}}},{title:{zh:"依赖结构决定定理能否使用",en:"Dependence determines whether the theorem applies"},body:{zh:"原始定理在独立检验统计量的条件下给出控制结果，并进一步说明证明所需的独立性范围。金融研究中重叠样本与相似变量容易导致检验相关。不能因为软件能够运行BH程序，就推断任意相关结构下都得到原文保证。",en:"The original theorem establishes control under independence and clarifies the independence needed by its proof. Overlapping financial samples and similar predictors often create dependent tests. Software successfully running the BH procedure does not establish the guarantee under arbitrary dependence."},reference:{url:"https://www.dcscience.net/Benjamini-Hochberg-1995-FDR.pdf",label:{zh:"1995年期刊版 · §3.1 · Theorem 1",en:"1995 journal article · §3.1 · Theorem 1"}}},{title:{zh:"检验家族要包括实际尝试的问题",en:"The testing family must reflect the questions actually tried"},body:{zh:"文中把待检验的假设视为事先已知，并把筛选后的确认研究视为重要使用情境。编辑建议：记录所有尝试而不只记录最终入选者，否则m不再描述真实选择空间。控制多重检验也不替代新样本验证、经济解释或数据质量检查。",en:"The framework treats the hypotheses as specified in advance and discusses screening before confirmation. Editorial application: record attempted hypotheses, not only selected ones, so m represents the testing family. Multiplicity control does not replace new-sample validation or sound measurement."},reference:{url:"https://www.dcscience.net/Benjamini-Hochberg-1995-FDR.pdf",label:{zh:"1995年期刊版 · §2; §2.2",en:"1995 journal article · §2; §2.2"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"FDR控制的是错误发现比例的期望，不是每次实验的错误比例保证，也不是单个发现为假的概率。1995年定理不能直接推广到任意相关的检验。",en:"FDR controls an expected false-discovery proportion, not a guarantee for each experiment or a posterior probability for one finding. The 1995 theorem does not cover arbitrary dependence."}};export{e as default};
